<header><h1>Action Cards</h1></header>
<article>
<h2>Rules Reference</h2>
<style> .lrr > li:before, .lrr > h2 > li:before {content: '2.' counter(item, decimal);} </style>
<p data-src="1,3">Action cards provide players with various abilities that they can resolve as described on the cards.</p>
    <ol class="lrr">
    <li data-src="1,3">Each player draws one action card during each status phase.</li>
    <li data-src="1,3">Players can draw action cards by resolving the primary and secondary abilities of the <a href="/R_politics"><i>Politics</i></a> strategy card.</li>
    <li data-src="1,3">When a player draws an action card, they take the top card from the action card deck and add it to their hand of action cards.</li>
    <li data-src="1,2,3">Each player&rsquo;s hand can have a maximum of <b>seven action cards</b>. If a player ever has more than seven action cards, that player must choose seven cards to keep and discard the rest.</li>
    <ol><li data-src="1">A game effect can increase or decrease the number of cards a player&rsquo;s hand can have.</li></ol>
    <li data-src="1">A player&rsquo;s action cards remain hidden from other players until those cards are played.</li>
    <li data-src="1,3">The first paragraph of each action card is presented in bold text and describes the timing of when that card&rsquo;s ability can be resolved.</li>
    <ol>
        <li data-src="1,2,3">If an action card contains the word &ldquo;Action&rdquo;, a player must use a component action during the action phase to resolve the ability. A player cannot resolve a component action if they cannot completely resolve its ability.</li>
        <li data-src="1,2">Multiple action cards with the <b>same</b> name cannot be played during a single timing window to affect the same units or game effect. Canceled cards are not treated as being played.</li>
    </ol>
    <li data-src="1,3">To play an action card, a player reads and resolves the card&rsquo;s ability text, making any decisions as prompted by the card. Then, that player discards the card, placing it in the action discard pile.</li>
    <li data-src="1">If an action card is canceled, that card has no effect and is discarded.</li>
    </ol>
<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Players start the game with zero action cards.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The number of action cards in a player&rsquo;s hand is public information.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A player may choose to reveal any or all of the action cards in their hand.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>If the action card deck is depleted, immediately shuffle the discard pile to form a new action card deck.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>During the status phase, action cards are drawn in initiative order, though this rarely matters in practice.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If a player has the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#Neural_Motivator"><i>Neural Motivator</i></a> technology, they will draw both their action cards before the next player in order draws an action card.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>The <a href="/F_yssaril">Yssaril</a> player will draw all of their action cards, and discard for their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Yssaril_Tribes#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Scheming"><sc>Scheming</sc></a> ability, before the next player in order draws an action card.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s action card is canceled, usually via a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Sabotage"><i>Sabotage</i></a> action card, then if that player has a second copy of that action card, they may play it.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>A player cannot use action cards that destroy units, such as <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Lucky%20Shot"><i>Lucky Shot</i></a>, against their own units.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card targets &ldquo;each&rdquo; of a particular type of object, that action card may target zero of those objects. As such, these cards may be played even if they would cause no effect.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card targets a specific number of a particular type of object, that action card cannot be played if those objects do not currently exist. For example, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Repeal%20Law"><i>Repeal Law</i></a> cannot be played if there are no laws in play.<sup>5</sup></li>
    <!-- <li>If a player has more than seven action cards, they must discard the excess.<sup>1,2,3</sup></li> -->
    <li>Action cards are discarded faceup. Players may look through the action card discard pile.<sup>2,4,5</sup></li>
    </ol>
